<http://data.silknow.org/object/d6ca7cf8-2edb-36bf-ad39-d1638694437b/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The netting of neutral violet silk is worked with gold and silver thread (thin strips of metal wound on silk). The design consists of the monogram I. H. S. in a field of stars and rosettes. At one end are the words \"Clemens Octavus\", at the other \"Pontifex Maximus.\" (He was Pope from 1592-1605.) Surrounding this is a border of leaves and acorns. Mounted on neutral violet silk and edged with gold lace into which has been run a thin strip of gold."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/d6ca7cf8-2edb-36bf-ad39-d1638694437b> .

